This development builds on Charlie Reams’s Lean formalization of Harald Andrés Helfgott’s ternary Goldbach theorem. The following notice is reproduced from that formalization.

Ternary Goldbach in Lean 4
Copyright 2026 Charlie Reams

A formalization of H. A. Helfgott's proof of the ternary Goldbach conjecture
(H. A. Helfgott, "The ternary Goldbach problem", arXiv:1501.05438).
Canonical repository: https://github.com/calr3/ternary-goldbach

TernaryGoldbach/Prelim/PNTMertens.lean is derived from the PrimeNumberTheoremAnd
project (https://github.com/AlexKontorovich/PrimeNumberTheoremAnd), licensed under
the Apache License 2.0.

The final theorem uses Levent Alpöge’s RH and primitive Dirichlet GRH declarations from the compiled release hosted by Proofs & Reasons. The replay manifest also identifies four source files from Steve Hubbard’s goldbach-lean project, fetched at the pinned revision during replay.

The statement above describes the historical release. The earlier Lean 4.37 port referenced the community GRH Git source as an external Lake dependency. The four Hubbard sources and their license and notice are included.

This branch targets Lean 4.35.0 using the grh-compact package at community mirror commit 72fead102f663d5c7a407964a13dc0cf9d977207. The embedded source notice in Main credits Levent Alpöge with Claude.

The compact source tree distributed in this package is accompanied by CompactGRH/LICENSE, CompactGRH/NOTICE and CompactGRH/ATTRIBUTION.md. The local module headers and public imports provide compatibility with the Goldbach modules.
